From: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ext_authz: http check timeout 10 s instead of 200 ms

In http mode the authorization call gets a fixed 200 ms timeout, and the
extAuthz block's policies (requestTimeout) are not passed to it at this
revision, so the timeout cannot be raised from the config. tactiq-stop,
the agent stop service TactiQ OS puts behind extAuthz, signs every
refusal with the TPM and took 2.4 s on the reference board: at 200 ms the
gateway denies on its own and the caller never receives the signed
receipt. Measured on the bench 26.10.2026.

Upstream main (October 2026) passes the policies to this call and
defaults to 2 s. Drop this patch when the recipe moves to such a revision
and the config's requestTimeout takes effect.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [superseded upstream by passing the extAuthz policies]
Signed-off-by: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
---
diff --git a/crates/agentgateway/src/http/ext_authz.rs b/crates/agentgateway/src/http/ext_authz.rs
index 523aabb..ef2b76c 100644
--- a/crates/agentgateway/src/http/ext_authz.rs
+++ b/crates/agentgateway/src/http/ext_authz.rs
@@ -605,10 +605,13 @@ impl ExtAuthz {
 			let resv = http::HeaderOrPseudoValue::from_cel_result(hn, res);
 			http::RequestOrResponse::Request(&mut check_req).apply_header(hn, resv, false);
 		}
-		// Set the default request timeout. This can be overridden by a timeout on the Backend object itself.
+		// TactiQ OS: 10 s instead of 200 ms. In http mode this timeout cannot be
+		// overridden at this revision (the extAuthz policies are not passed to
+		// the call below), and tactiq-stop needs about 2.4 s to sign a refusal
+		// on an SPI TPM. Upstream main passes the policies and defaults to 2 s.
 		check_req
 			.extensions_mut()
-			.insert(BackendRequestTimeout(Duration::from_millis(200)));
+			.insert(BackendRequestTimeout(Duration::from_secs(10)));
 		let resp = client.call_reference(check_req, &self.target).await;
 		let mut resp = match resp {
 			Ok(r) => r,
